{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.bond_character_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.bond_character_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L219-L237","doc":"**The bond's CHARACTER deviates at fourth order, not second.** From step 4's\n`trace_vtx_pow_three`, `χ_(2,1)(V³) − 2 = −h⁴·(3 + h²)`, because `tr D = −3h² − h⁴` is itself\n`O(h²)`. The *matrix* deviation is `h²`; the *character* deviation is `h⁴`.\n\n**CORRECTED (step 10, `DiprotonResponseClosedForm`).** This docstring continued: \"the interface\nratio is controlled by the matrix, since `tr(W·D)` carries no such cancellation — so checking\nthe order on characters gives the wrong answer for the binding.\" **The second clause is false.**\nExact symbolic evaluation of the `H₆` convention-D Markov trace on the two 11-letter nucleon\nwords gives `r = h²·c(q)` with `c` order one, so `tr(W·D)` *does* carry a cancellation and the\nratio deviates at `h⁴`, not `h²`. A single block's mixed response carries one factor `q² − 1`;\nthe second appears only after `y`-weighting. So there are three distinct orders here (matrix\n`h²`, per-block mixed response `h¹`, `y`-weighted response `h²`, hence ratio `h⁴`) and the\n`h⁴` below agrees with the ratio's `h⁴` by arithmetic rather than by mechanism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.response_bounded_of_deviation_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.response_bounded_of_deviation_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L202-L217","doc":"**The relative response is bounded independently of `h`.** If the numerator `tr(W·D)` is\nbounded by `K` and the free trace is bounded away from zero by `m > 0`, then `|r| ≤ K/m` — a\nbound with no `h` in it. This is what makes `binding_magnitude_second_order` a statement about\na *scale*: without it, `r := (μ − 1)/h²` is a definition and the bracket is vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.deviation_coefficient_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.deviation_coefficient_le","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L196-L200","doc":"**The deviation's coefficient is bounded on the interval.** `D = (2 + h²)·V + 1`, and on\n`h² ≤ 1/10` the scalar factor is at most `21/10` — an `h`-free bound, so `D`'s size is\ncontrolled by `V`'s alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.bound_on_q_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.bound_on_q_interval","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L183-L192","doc":"The same statement at the proton pin's bound, written on `q` so the chain from the\nsubstrate modulus to the order is visible: `1 < q ≤ 23/20` forces the `h²` ceiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.bound_at_small_h_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.bound_at_small_h_sq","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L168-L181","doc":"**On the arc's own interval.** For `h² ≤ 1/10` — which `1 < q ≤ 23/20` guarantees\n(`h_sq_le_of_q_le`, step 4) and the proton pin satisfies with `h² ≈ 0.0437` — the magnitude\nis at most `α·r/10`. With `α = 𝔈₀^full ≈ 4.23` MeV and a response of order `10⁻²`, that is a\nkeV-scale ceiling derived rather than observed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.binding_negative_of_pos_response","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.binding_negative_of_pos_response","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L160-L166","doc":"**The sign, from step 8's law.** A positive relative response — the bond moves the\ninterface trace upward — makes the binding negative, i.e. unbound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.binding_magnitude_second_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.binding_magnitude_second_order","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L132-L158","doc":"**The headline: the binding magnitude is `Θ(h²)`.** With a positive scale `α`, a\nnon-zero deformation `h`, and a positive relative response `r`, the magnitude of\n`B = −α·log(1 + h²r)` satisfies\n\n    α·h²r / (1 + h²r)  ≤  |B|  ≤  α·h²r.\n\nBoth bounds carry `h²`, so the magnitude is exactly second order in the deformation — the\nstructural reason a γγ-selected interface bond moves a binding by keV rather than MeV, given\nan `α` of a few MeV. No constant is chosen anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.ratio_eq_one_add_of_linear_response","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.ratio_eq_one_add_of_linear_response","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L122-L128","doc":"**The bookkeeping step.** If the interface trace is linear in the bond — `tr(W·(1 + M))\n= tr W + tr (W·M)`, which the Markov trace is — and the bond's deviation is `h² • D`, then\nthe ratio is `1 + h²·r` with `r` the relative response `tr(W·D)/tr W`. Stated on the\nscalars, so it applies block by block and to the weighted sum alike. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.vertexCube_deviation_is_h_sq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.vertexCube_deviation_is_h_sq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L112-L120","doc":"**Re-export of step 4's cube identity**: the `(2,1)` image of the selected bond\n`G³ = (σ₂σ₃⁻¹)³` differs from the identity by exactly `h²` times a matrix built from the\nvertex. The exponent is forced by the Hoefsmit relations; nothing is chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.le_log_one_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.le_log_one_add","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L100-L108","doc":"`x/(1+x) ≤ log(1 + x)` for `x > -1`. Together with `log_one_add_le` this brackets\n`log(1+x)` between two quantities of the same order in `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.log_one_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder.log_one_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonSecondOrder.lean#L94-L98","doc":"`log(1 + x) ≤ x` for `x > -1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}